{
  "post_stream": {
    "posts": [
      {
        "id": 2777110,
        "name": "Peter Powers",
        "username": "Peter_Powers",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.eveonline.com/peter_powers/{size}/483239_2.png",
        "created_at": "2025-09-22T07:59:52.131Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hi, some of you might remember me from a few years ago, i recently returned to EVE,<br>\nand I was suprised to see how little has been happening around AI tooling (both on EVE side, as well as on 3rd party side).</p>\n<p>Example: for a recent Event I got an Evemail by Mordus and couldn’t even reply to it, where as its pretty easy to have an LLM do roleplay answers. Come on CCP you can do better.</p>\n<p>Anyways,<br>\nI’ve for a long time been using the EVE API / the 3rd party ecosystem to explore technologies I’m familiarising myself with (those old Enough might remember me speaking about a Killboard with MongoDB on Fanfest a decade ago..).</p>\n<p>So i’ve done it again, to explore and learn Automation with n8n, graph databases and working with LLM better, I’ve picked a usecase and build a small App.</p>\n<p>The App: <a href=\"https://everyshore.battlefield.space\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://everyshore.battlefield.space</a> is an automated tool that watches and analyses activity in the Everyshore region, building advisories and character profiles.</p>\n<p>You can find a bit more about the Stack used on <a href=\"https://everyshore.battlefield.space/about\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">About – Everyshore Intelligence Network</a><br>\nIts not perfect (yet <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/wink.png?v=14\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> ) but I think its a good way of show casing how a bit of creative thinking can build pretty amazing tools around this game.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "posts_count": 1,
        "updated_at": "2025-09-22T07:59:52.131Z",
